{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793555304,"nonce":"PLLiKi/CMQpwB8gntF4bq33rYFo=","message":"Layer 1 (snapshot publish) is built and committed. A restored browser session has a Save to cloud action: the Worker mints an HMAC-signed, expiring capability each time it prepares a synced workspace and sends it to the runner (never stored); the runner puts it in the session's environment with the gateway, workspace and restored generation; the session answers sync.publish by scanning its tree without git (scan_tree, honouring the tree's own .gitignore, carrying the previous manifest's git section over) and publishing the next generation. The capability reads and publishes only its own workspace as its owner. A save against a stale base is a conflict and overwrites nothing; verified end to end through the real session and in the browser panel.\n\nStill open: layer 2 (text edits as Yrs updates). Also: a sandboxed runner must be allowed to reach the gateway for a save to work (the msb network allowlist); the session's token is removed from the programs and terminals it starts but is visible to the session process itself; saves are whole-tree scans with no unsaved-buffer capture yet; the panel offers Save only, there is no pull of newer cloud generations into a running session.","files":null}]}